%==================== 2. OVERALL DESCRIPTION ====================
\chapter{Overall Description}

\section{Product Perspective}
SAMS evolves the existing prototype rather than replacing it. It keeps the layered (three-layer) architecture and the technology stack, and adds new modules on top of the existing ones. The system remains a \textbf{modular monolith}: all modules share one backend and one database, while access is controlled by the API.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Presentation layer} --- one React single-page application containing the public portal, the passenger \emph{My Journey} pages, the department workspaces and the administrator workspace.
    \item \textbf{Application/API layer} --- a Node.js/Express REST API. Every protected request passes through authentication and authorization middleware before reaching controllers and services. New services handle events, impact rules, notifications, action items, approvals, escalation and audit logging.
    \item \textbf{Data layer} --- MongoDB accessed through Mongoose. The browser never accesses the database directly.
\end{enumerate}

