\subsection*{Roles and Access}
SAMS applies role-based access control (RBAC), extended with departments. A \textbf{role} defines what a person may do; a \textbf{department} defines the operational area they belong to. A user account has one role and, for staff and supervisors, one department. For example, a baggage employee is \emph{Department Staff} in \emph{Baggage Handling}; a baggage supervisor belongs to the same department with additional supervisory permissions.

\begin{longtable}{L{3.0cm} L{3.4cm} L{8.0cm}}
\toprule
\textbf{User class} & \textbf{Access method} & \textbf{Responsibilities and access} \\ \midrule \endhead
\bottomrule \endfoot
Public user & No login & Views published flights, announcements and transport information only. \\
Passenger & Optional passenger sign-in & Public information plus own registered journeys, own baggage details and own notifications. No access to internal records or other passengers' data. \\
Department Staff & Common staff login & Creates and updates authorized records and fields of the assigned department; views relevant shared summaries; receives and acknowledges notifications; works on assigned tasks. \\
Department Supervisor & Same login, added permissions & Staff permissions plus team task assignment, departmental oversight, receipt of overdue-task escalations, and approval of explicitly delegated changes. \\
Central Administrator & Same login, role-based redirect & Cross-department overview, incident monitoring, designated approvals, account and role/department administration within granted permissions, rule-based escalations. \\
Super Administrator & Restricted technical access & Global roles, permissions and system configuration (impact and escalation rules). Not an operational department; may be omitted from the initial demonstration. \\
\end{longtable}

\noindent The role values used in the prototype are mapped to the new user classes as follows, so that existing accounts keep working: \texttt{admin} $\rightarrow$ Central Administrator; \texttt{airline\_staff} $\rightarrow$ Department Staff (Flight Operations); \texttt{staff} $\rightarrow$ Department Staff (Baggage Handling); \texttt{transport\_operator} $\rightarrow$ Department Staff (Ground Transport); \texttt{passenger} $\rightarrow$ Passenger. The prototype's \texttt{visitor} login role is retired, because public information no longer requires an account.

