\section{Product Functions}
At a high level, SAMS provides the following functions (detailed in Chapter~\ref{ch:features}):
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Authentication and account management} --- passenger self-registration, common staff login, role-based redirection, administrator-controlled roles and departments.
    \item \textbf{Authorization and record scope} --- checks by role, department, resource and field on every protected request.
    \item \textbf{Operational management} --- flights, luggage/baggage, baggage issues, visitors, staff and transportation.
    \item \textbf{Public portal and passenger journeys} --- public information without login; optional personal journeys and alerts.
    \item \textbf{Events, notifications and action items} --- automatic, rule-based coordination between departments.
    \item \textbf{Approval workflow} --- sensitive changes stay pending until approved.
    \item \textbf{Incident and audit timeline} --- the full, persisted history of each incident.
    \item \textbf{Overdue-task escalation} --- supervisor alerts and rule-based escalation to central administration.
    \item \textbf{Role-aware dashboards and reports} --- database-derived values; demonstration data clearly labelled.
\end{itemize}

