\section{User Documentation}
The repository will contain a \texttt{README} covering installation, environment configuration, seeding demonstration data and running the backend and frontend, plus a short user guide for each workspace. This SRS and the project report serve as the requirements and design documentation.

\section{Assumptions and Dependencies}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Passenger-specific notifications depend on registered journeys and a reliable link between passenger accounts, flights and baggage records.
    \item A flight delay alone does not prove that a connecting passenger will miss a connection; the system must not present an unconfirmed outcome as fact.
    \item Public endpoints expose only approved public fields; internal incidents and personal data remain protected.
    \item The Central Administrator account and the department list are created (seeded) before the system is demonstrated.
    \item A MongoDB instance is available and reachable from the backend.
    \item New capabilities are planned requirements and must not be described as implemented until they are verified and tested.
\end{itemize}

