\section{Functional Requirements}

\subsection{F1 --- Authentication and Account Management}
\textbf{Stimulus/response:} A user signs in on the common login page; the server verifies the credentials, issues a JSON Web Token (JWT), and the frontend opens the workspace for the verified role and department.
\begin{reqtable}
FR-1.1 & The system shall support login, logout and retrieval of the authenticated user's profile (\texttt{GET /api/auth/me}). & High & Implemented \\
FR-1.2 & Public self-registration shall create Passenger accounts only; the server shall ignore or reject any client-supplied role. & High & Planned \\
FR-1.3 & Privileged roles and department assignments shall be created and changed only by authorized administrators. & High & Planned \\
FR-1.4 & The system shall keep the existing JWT and bcrypt-based authentication, with secrets held in environment configuration. & High & Implemented \\
FR-1.5 & After a successful staff or administrator login, the frontend shall redirect the user to the workspace for the verified role and department. & High & Planned \\
FR-1.6 & The backend shall reject invalid or expired tokens (implemented) and accounts marked inactive (planned: requires an \texttt{active} flag on users). & High & Partial \\
FR-1.7 & The JWT shall carry the user's ID, role and department; the server shall reload the user's current role, department and active state for privileged operations so that revoked access takes effect immediately. & Medium & Planned \\
\end{reqtable}

\subsection{F2 --- Authorization and Record Scope}
\textbf{Stimulus/response:} Every protected request is checked for a valid token, then for role, department, record scope and permitted fields, before any data is read or changed. Role checks follow the RBAC model; department, record and field checks refine it.
\begin{reqtable}
FR-2.1 & Every protected API operation shall enforce authorization on the backend; hiding a frontend control alone shall not be relied on for security. & High & Implemented \\
FR-2.2 & Authorization shall consider role, department, resource scope and permitted fields. Role checks are currently implemented; department, scope and field checks are planned. & High & Partial \\
FR-2.3 & A department shall be able to edit only the record types and fields it owns (Table~\ref{tab:perm}); read access shall not imply edit access. & High & Planned \\
FR-2.4 & Passengers shall access only their own journeys, their own baggage information and explicitly public data. & High & Planned \\
FR-2.5 & Users shall not be able to change their own role or department by submitting modified request fields. & High & Planned \\
FR-2.6 & Unauthorized requests shall return HTTP 401 (not authenticated) or 403 (not permitted) without changing stored data. & High & Implemented \\
FR-2.7 & The permission matrix in Table~\ref{tab:perm} shall be defined in one server-side configuration so that it can be reviewed and tested as a whole. & Medium & Planned \\
\end{reqtable}

