\subsection{F6 --- Approval Workflow}
\label{sec:approval}
\textbf{Sensitive changes} in the MVP are: cancelling a flight; changing a departure time by more than 60 minutes; deleting a flight or transport record; and assigning or changing a privileged role or department. Other valid, authorized changes are \textbf{routine} and apply immediately.
\begin{reqtable}
FR-6.1 & Routine changes shall be applied immediately when the user is authorized and the change is valid. & High & Planned \\
FR-6.2 & Sensitive changes shall be stored as pending change requests and shall not alter the authoritative record until approved. & High & Planned \\
FR-6.3 & Approval and rejection shall record the reviewer, decision, timestamp and, for rejections, a reason. & High & Planned \\
FR-6.4 & An urgent change may bypass prior approval only under an explicitly configured policy and permission; the system shall record the reason and require a later review. & Medium & Planned \\
FR-6.5 & A user shall not be able to approve their own change request. & Medium & Planned \\
FR-6.6 & An approved change request shall be applied through the same validation as a direct update, and shall generate the corresponding event. & High & Planned \\
\end{reqtable}

\subsection{F7 --- Incident and Audit Timeline}
\begin{reqtable}
FR-7.1 & For each incident, the system shall show a chronological timeline of the report, related events, notifications, acknowledgements, decisions, approvals, task updates and resolution. & High & Planned \\
FR-7.2 & Important changes shall record the acting user, action, entity, timestamp and before/after values where appropriate. & High & Planned \\
FR-7.3 & Audit records shall be append-only for ordinary users and readable only by authorized roles. & High & Planned \\
FR-7.4 & The timeline shall distinguish notification acknowledgement, task completion and incident resolution. & High & Planned \\
FR-7.5 & The timeline shall be built from persisted records, not hard-coded demonstration events. & High & Planned \\
\end{reqtable}

\subsection{F8 --- Overdue-Task Escalation}
\begin{reqtable}
FR-8.1 & Action items may have a due time and a priority-based escalation rule. & High & Planned \\
FR-8.2 & When a task passes its due time without resolution, the system shall mark it \emph{Overdue} and notify the responsible department supervisor. & High & Planned \\
